WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.260
Fine, fine.

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:04.450
Since everyone won’t stop asking, I’ve
decided to give you all what you want and

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:07.840
do a Horror History episode on Wyborn Lovat
from Coraline.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.120
And the truth is, Wybie was only created for
the movie.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:13.670
He’s not in the book at all, so he technically
has no history.

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:18.040
So remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, RING that deathbell--

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:22.650
No, I’ll obviously have to go off of the
movie and the movie alone for this episode,

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:26.090
but if you want to hear what goes on with
Wybie while he's off screen then stick around

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:28.140
to the end of this video.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:31.800
[INTRO]

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.600
Part of what makes the world of Coraline special
is that the artistic choices made reflect

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:36.879
the themes of the story.

00:00:36.879 --> 00:00:40.640
The book tells a tale of a girl who finds
this fake world and is intrigued by the small

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.190
differences it has to her world.

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:45.659
I like to think of the film as a whole, as
it’s own world to be treated differently

00:00:45.659 --> 00:00:49.679
than the book, and the most noticeable difference,
the snowglobe of the film, if you will, is

00:00:49.679 --> 00:00:51.050
the inclusion of Wybie.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:55.239
Welcome to Horror History, my name is Why-Was-I-Born
and in today’s lesson we’ll be covering

00:00:55.239 --> 00:00:59.159
the character who probably owns the most Jack
Skellington merch, Wyborn Lovat.

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:02.609
Of course, there is a much more practical
reason for Wybie’s inclusion, as explained

00:01:02.609 --> 00:01:05.170
by director Henry Selick in an interview with
Cinemablend.

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:09.189
“[When I decided to add the character of
Wybie] I realized that Coraline needed someone

00:01:09.189 --> 00:01:10.990
in her real world to talk to.

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:12.940
Another kid seemed the most simple way to
go.”

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:16.740
But the character that ended up on screen
was much more than a glorified exposition

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:20.620
prompter, so in order to understand Wybie’s
importance to the lore and history of this

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:23.760
dark, twisted world, let’s take it back
to the beginning of his story.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:31.060
Wybie looks to be about Coraline’s age,
and lives with his Grandma in a property not

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.560
far from the Pink Palace Apartments where
Coraline lives.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:37.229
It is not known what happened to his parents,
but we do know the fate of his Great Aunt.

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:40.480
She once lived with Wybie’s grandmother
in the Pink Palace before it was converted

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:41.820
into separate apartments.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:44.999
As discussed in the Horror History episode
on The Other Mother, living at the Pink Palace

00:01:44.999 --> 00:01:46.640
made her a target for the Beldam.

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:50.310
In the movie, the Beldam spies on her potential
victims through the eyes of this doll, which

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.950
is placed in the real world for the children
to find.

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:56.100
Wybie’s Great-Aunt became attached to the
doll, and one day she disappeared and became

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.600
trapped in the Beldam’s world.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:01.380
I think Wybie’s Grandmother suspected some
foul play, because she moved out of the Palace

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:05.210
when she was old enough, and when it became
hers, she renovated it into apartments, and

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:08.440
didn’t allow families with children to move
there until the events of Coraline.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:12.320
We don’t know why Coraline is an exception
of this rule, but there one line to suggest

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:16.190
that she simply had to rent the place to the
Joneses because of anti age discrimination

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:17.190
laws.

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:19.400
“Surprised she let you move in.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.610
My Grandma, she owns The Pink Palace.

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:23.420
She won’t rent to people with kids.”

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:25.360
“What do you mean?”

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.730
“Well, I’m not supposed to talk about
it.”

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:31.190
On a side note, Wybie’s grandma is referred
to as ‘Grandma’ through most of the movie

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:33.530
and ‘Wybie’s Grandmother’ in the credits.

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:36.150
At one point, Coraline refers to her as Ms.
Lovat.

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:37.870
“Welcome Ms. Lovat.”

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:41.880
The woman doesn’t correct Coraline, so by
that logic, it was her son that was Wybie’s

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.640
father, passing down the last name Lovat all
the way to him.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:48.450
The fact that she is Ms. Lovat rather than
Mrs. Lovat also suggests that she gave birth

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:51.560
to Wybie’s dad out of wedlock, meaning that
Wybie’s grandfather hasn’t been part of

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.450
the picture for some time now.

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:56.720
It’s also possible that Coraline just didn’t
know whether to call her Ms. or Mrs.

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:00.890
“I thought we got past that, but this guy
wants to bring it back.”

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:04.100
After the disappearance of her sister, she
locked the doll away in a chest, until it

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:07.720
was reclaimed by the Beldam and turned into
a Coraline doll, where it was then put back

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.560
in the chest for Wybie to find.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:13.290
Other than exploring the area around his house
on his electric bicycle, Wybie seems to be

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:14.800
passionate about photography.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:18.560
He makes friends with a wild cat, which he
sometimes feeds in exchange for the dead things

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:19.980
that cat brings him at night.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:23.480
He first encounters Coraline after she moves
in when he hears he scream after the cat had

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:24.480
startled her.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:27.510
He approaches and mistakes her for a water
witch, and rides in to take the stick that

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:29.170
he perceives to be her dowsing rod.

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:33.450
When they meet, we see that despite his intimidating
appearance, he’s actually pretty shy, oftentimes

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:35.450
stuttering and avoiding eye contact.

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:39.300
His hunched over posture does not exude confidence,
which coupled with the information that kids

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:43.160
are never usually moved into The Pink Palace,
we can conclude that he doesn’t have any

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.030
friends… other than The Cat that is.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:47.440
Coraline has this same issue at the beginning
of the story.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:51.120
She’s constantly bored and none of the adults
around her have time to play with her.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:54.360
Despite this, Coraline and Wybie don’t really
get along when they first meet.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:57.530
Wybie does tell her about the location of
the well though, before his Grandmother calls

00:03:57.530 --> 00:04:00.090
him in, ringing a bell for him as she does
so.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:01.280
“Wyborn?”

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:02.470
“Grandma...”

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:05.730
Wybie seems embarrassed by his Grandmother’s
strict control over his whereabouts.

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:09.350
I believe this may be because after all of
these years, she’s still scarred by losing

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:13.100
her sister, and fears the same could happen
to her grandson if he gets too close to The

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:14.190
Pink Palace.

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:16.640
As a result, Wybie has never been inside the
building.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:18.209
“Grandma’d kill me.”

00:04:18.209 --> 00:04:22.220
So he goes home and finds the doll, which
he recognizes to be identical to Coraline

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:23.880
and leaves it on her porch with a note.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:27.440
The next morning he’s snooping around and
spies on her using some kind of Periscope

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:28.440
helmet.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:30.400
When she catches him he claims to be hunting
banana slugs.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:33.820
Director Henry Selick may have gone with banana
slugs as the creature of choice to setup what

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:36.280
happens to The Other Wybie later in the story.

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:39.530
Coraline claims to be annoyed by Wybie because
of his loud mouth, causing The Other Mother

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:41.870
to create a mute version of him in the other
world.

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:45.230
Banana slugs have a defense mechanism where
the mucus that they release contains chemicals

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:47.900
that are capable of numbing the tongue of
their predators.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:51.470
Despite Coraline claiming to not like Wybie,
she does still seem to enjoy taking the photos

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:53.810
of him in various poses with the banana slug.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:57.520
Outside of one other encounter with Coraline
where Wybie claims that Mr Bobinsky's jumping

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:01.900
mouse circus is a lie, the two would not encounter
each other until the next day, but Coraline does

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:05.220
meet his doppelganger, The Other Wybie.

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:15.170
As we established when I covered the history
of The Other Mother, the button-eyed doppelganger

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:18.960
forms of each character found in the other
world aren't really connected to their real-world

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:19.960
counterparts.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:23.650
However, the duplicate versions can still
teach us about the nature of the originals,

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:26.890
because the Other Mother's intention was to
create more enticing forms of the people in

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:28.150
Coraline's life.

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:31.880
As with the Other Father the Other Wybie seems
to have a mind of his own, and only acts the

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:33.480
way he does out of fear for The Beldam.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:37.980
In addition to being friendly and incapable
of speech, he's also less shy, stands up straight

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:39.560
and wears more conventional clothing.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:43.250
He seems to be a more ideal version of Wybie
to be friends with Coraline, but like the

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:47.160
endless amounts of delicious food and freedom
offered by the Beldam's world, Other Wybie

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:51.270
ends up being another example of things being
better off as they were initially.

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:54.840
Coraline maybe doesn't realize how lonely
she is, and having a friend who doesn't talk

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:56.860
isn't doing her any favors in that regard.

00:05:56.860 --> 00:06:00.419
One of the first things that Coraline asks
him, is if the treatment to make him silent

00:06:00.419 --> 00:06:04.020
caused him any pain, and he immediately changes
the subject, probably knowing that he is under

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:05.910
constant scrutiny by The Other Mother.

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:09.460
The two go to see the jumping mouse circus,
the very same jumping mouse circus that the

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:11.210
real Wybie called BS on.

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:14.480
After seeing Coraline off to bed before she
exits from The Other World that night, The

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:17.700
Other Wybie shows that he really does have
good intentions by warning The Cat about the

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:19.810
true nature of the Other World.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:23.740
Coraline returns to her world, and while Wybie
isn’t there the next day when Mr. and Mrs.

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:27.669
Jones take their daughter into town to buy
a uniform, there are other kids in that scene,

00:06:27.669 --> 00:06:29.250
which tells us two things.

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:32.940
First, Coraline shows no interest in meeting
them despite her loneliness, because of their

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:36.650
erratic behaviour, which could be a clue that
the often awkward and reserved Wybie could

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:38.970
actually be a more compatible friendship for
her.

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:42.420
She may have gotten the wrong idea about him
from their initial meeting.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:46.280
And second, there ARE other kids nearby, so
the fact that we never see Wybie play with

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:50.150
or talk about any other kids could mean that
he has no friends, and maybe I’m assuming

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:53.840
too much by saying this, but it’s easy to
imagine him being bullied for his outlandish

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:56.280
fashion choices and unconventional hobbies.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:07:01.180
The Other Wybie, on the other hand, pun intended,
is copied from the original Wybie, but changed

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:03.320
in ways that The Beldam thought to be improvements.

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:05.790
Both versions seem to like Coraline and want
to help her.

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:09.220
In the case of the Other Wybie, The Beldam
may have made him friendly and likeable because

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:11.510
her goal was to try to make Coraline want
to stay.

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:15.260
She probably didn’t realize that Other Wybie’s
good intentions would be used against her.

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:18.740
I could see her thinking that making him mute
would stop him from helping Coraline in any

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:20.640
way, but that ends up not being the case.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:23.770
The Other Wybie is forced to accompany her
to the theater… where he has a very weird

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:26.560
reaction to seeing the nearly naked Miss Forcible…

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:31.210
He keeps up the cheery attitude until he is
no longer needed.

00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:34.330
As Coraline goes inside, The Other Mother
gives him a harsh reminder that he needs to

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:37.830
keep on a smile the whole time, despite the
fact that he’s clearly unhappy.

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:41.669
While Coraline is locked away in the mirror
realm, The Other Mother punishes Other Wybie

00:07:41.669 --> 00:07:42.950
for his insubordination.

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:47.090
She uses her seamstress abilities to tie his
mouth into a permanent smile, ensuring that

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:49.570
he’ll never give Coraline any negative energy
towards Coraline.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:52.800
It’s basically like when you go to a fast
food restaurant and the person at the counter

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:57.030
is smiling because they don’t want to get
fired, but deep down they probably are like,

00:07:57.030 --> 00:07:58.500
“someone get me out of here.”

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:01.700
At this point, I think that Other Wybie has
been pushed to a breaking point.

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:04.790
He’s been brought into this world by the
Other Mother and forced to do her bidding.

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:07.580
He may not have had any hope for himself,
but thought that he could at least do the

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:10.820
brave thing and make sure Coraline doesn’t
share the same fate.

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:14.600
Ironically, he wears a chicken mask to cover
up his forced smile when he reaches into the

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:17.730
mirror realm to rescue her, and she removed
the cover up to find that The Other Wybie

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:18.920
was no chicken at all.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:21.990
He manages to sneak her back to the gateway
between the two worlds, but when she tries

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:25.729
to invite him to come along, his hand erodes
into the stuffing used to make the doll that

00:08:25.729 --> 00:08:27.680
was used to spy on each target.

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:31.070
I think this was his way of telling her that
he has no way to survive out there in the

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:32.070
real world.

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:35.730
He was just a tool created by The Beldam,
no different than the doll that Coraline had

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:36.740
discarded in the fire.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:40.849
We never see The Other Wybie again after that,
but we can assume that he, no longer being

00:08:40.849 --> 00:08:43.240
useful to The Other Mother, was discarded
as well.

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:46.910
The Other Mother hangs his clothes on the
flagpole atop her world as a warning to all

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:50.020
of her other creations about what will happen
if they disobey her.

00:08:50.020 --> 00:08:53.649
Meanwhile, the original Wybie is still fine
and well, but he gets himself into a different

00:08:53.649 --> 00:08:54.660
kind of trouble.

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:58.420
His Grandmother is upset with him for stealing
the doll that had once belonged to her sister.

00:08:58.420 --> 00:09:01.620
Wybie tries to go back to Coraline’s flat
to ask for it, explaining that it wasn’t

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:05.399
his to give, and this causes Coraline to realize
that Ms. Lovat’s sister and the ghost girl

00:09:05.399 --> 00:09:07.279
she had encountered are one and the same.

00:09:07.279 --> 00:09:11.139
She brings Wybie inside, his first time setting
foot in The Pink Palace, and tries to explain

00:09:11.140 --> 00:09:15.180
everything that she knew about the Other World,
which of course sounds crazy.

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:16.380
“Crazy!

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:19.280
AHHHHHHH--”

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:22.939
...and she gets upset and chases him out,
but when he returned home, he would find something

00:09:22.939 --> 00:09:25.139
that changed his views on Coraline’s story.

00:09:25.139 --> 00:09:27.579
His Grandmother showed him a picture from
her childhood.

00:09:27.579 --> 00:09:31.360
The photograph shows Ms. Lovat and her sister,
who is holding the doll, which Wybie recognizes

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:32.529
from Coraline’s story.

00:09:32.529 --> 00:09:36.139
He rushes out to try to find her and apologize
for not believing her, and finds her headed

00:09:36.139 --> 00:09:37.319
back to the old well.

00:09:37.319 --> 00:09:41.480
Before he gets the chance to say anything,
she is attacked by the rogue hand of The Beldam.

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:45.129
Using the same tongs he uses to catch the
banana slugs, he rides in and saves her, but

00:09:45.129 --> 00:09:47.700
nearly throws himself into the well in doing
so.

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:50.759
Coraline saves him from falling in, but exposes
herself to an attack.

00:09:50.759 --> 00:09:54.800
That is when Wybie puts an end to it by crushing
the hand with a rock, rescuing Coraline and

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:58.360
finally avenging the Great Aunt he never met
in doing so.

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:02.080
Together, they throw the hand down the well,
and as far as we know, The Beldam is never

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:03.350
heard from again.

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:07.309
Wybie apologizes for not believing Coraline
sooner, but she isn’t upset, and asks him

00:10:07.309 --> 00:10:10.009
to bring his Grandma by the house so that
they can explain everything together.

00:10:10.009 --> 00:10:13.910
I took this ending as, not only an ending
to The Beldam’s reign (with The Cat being

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:17.641
seen taking advantage of the freedom to now
travel between worlds as he pleases), but

00:10:17.641 --> 00:10:21.759
also the ending of Ms. Lovat’s paranoia
about the curse of The Pink Palace and the

00:10:21.759 --> 00:10:23.149
children who inhabit it.

00:10:23.149 --> 00:10:26.990
She would finally be able to rest easy knowing
that her sister’s ghost was not in agony.

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:30.970
And finally, it marks the ending of loneliness
for both Coraline and Wybie, who now each

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:32.750
had a new friend their age.

